{"ts":"2026-09-05T18:24:36.441Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"grok-4.6","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"9b818639c0a44cda4607de9c","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"grok-4.6","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-05T18:24:36.441Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-05T18:24:36.441Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Pinned @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, pm-changelog ^2026.9.2, pm-ops 2026.9.5. The git item merge driver now uses conflictResolution=latest_document_update; preview still called mergeItemDocuments with the SDK default preferred_side, so the suite asserted ours-wins priority 1 while git merge retained the later updated_at (priority 3). Preview now passes the driver override. The test asserts the real merge matches the driver primitive and that this fixture actually distinguishes recency from ours-wins. Revert-proof: old assertion failed 1/0 (3 !== 1), restored test passed 1/0. Acceptance scripts and README use pm package install because install is the deprecated alias."}]}],"before_hash":"7916d99f92da7c407cf29828ed1ad56c1be1886c8a1a9e93828e0f0dd11f683f","after_hash":"840aca696c4bb2622c01f6360c1a992cba5342242d8fbf4bd826b2db2d705ddc","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c6728cd4ceec0c952bb74ca77c6be66fdcf041b0bc9cc325f70fef1ff03ba823"}
